ok - lifecycle wrappers use Bash without shell interpolation and preserve failure mapping
ok - POSIX lifecycle Bash resolution ignores an exported BASH
ok - N1: the host admits an inherited directory lifecycle lock and retires it without residue
ok - N2/N3: a host killed before, after or during its retirement leaves a lock the shell recovers
ok - N4: a paused host cannot retire a successor's directory lifecycle lock
ok - N5: a junk entry leaves only a husk after the host deletes its generation
ok - N6: an ambiguous directory record is rejected without retirement
